{"compatibility":"minor","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: minor.

Protected data: `obs`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

Changes: rewrote the observation model from indexed sampling statements inside a loop (`obs[i] ~ ...`) to a single top-level protected sampling statement (`obs ~ poisson_log(...)`) using a local predictor vector computed from context indices and parameters. Reordered priors so hyperparameters are sampled before being used in the prior for `alpha`. Added `sd_alpha ~ uniform(0, 5)`, matching the finite bounds on `sd_alpha` and making the implicit bounded uniform prior explicit for SafeStan. The data file is unchanged.
","model_safe_stan":"data {
  int<lower=0> nobs; // Number of observed data
  int<lower=0> nmis; // Number of missing data
  int<lower=0> nyear; // Number of years
  int<lower=0> nsite; // Number of sites
  array[nobs] int<lower=0> obs; // Observed counts
  array[nobs] int<lower=0> obsyear; // Years in observed data
  array[nobs] int<lower=0> obssite; // Sites in observed data
  array[nmis] int<lower=0> misyear; // Years in missing data
  array[nmis] int<lower=0> missite; // Sites in missing data
}
parameters {
  vector[nsite] alpha; // Random site effects
  real mu_alpha;
  real<lower=0, upper=5> sd_alpha;
}
transformed parameters {
  matrix[nyear, nsite] log_lambda;

  log_lambda = rep_matrix(alpha', nyear);
}
model {
  vector[nobs] log_lambda_obs;

  // Priors
  mu_alpha ~ normal(0, 10);
  sd_alpha ~ uniform(0, 5);
  alpha ~ normal(mu_alpha, sd_alpha);

  for (i in 1 : nobs) {
    log_lambda_obs[i] = log_lambda[obsyear[i], obssite[i]];
  }
  obs ~ poisson_log(log_lambda_obs);
}
generated quantities {
  array[nmis] int<lower=0> mis;

  for (i in 1 : nmis) {
    mis[i] = poisson_log_rng(log_lambda[misyear[i], missite[i]]);
  }
}
","data_safe_json":"{"missite":[1,2,3,2],"misyear":[1,4,2,4],"nmis":4,"nobs":2,"nsite":1,"nyear":4,"obs":[1,3],"obssite":[2,3],"obsyear":[3,3]}","protected_variables":["obs"]}
